  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Shown in the figure is a hollow ice-cream cone (it is open at top). If its mass is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>, radius of its top is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;and height,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>, then its moment of inertia about its axis is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0132_e056cc3c8877.png\" style=\"width: 152px; height: 260px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MH</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It can be assumed as several parts of discs having different radius, so</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0132_413e31a93f20.png\" style=\"width: 155px; height: 183px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>dl</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>dm</mi><mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math></p><p>From diagram</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mtext>&#952;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>y</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>dm</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>&#961;</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mtext>&#960;</mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>dy</mi></math></p><p>From equation (i), (ii) and (iii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
